<article class="env-lemma" id="085W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/085W">Lemma <span data-tag="085W">71.17.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. If $X$ is reduced, then the blowup $X'$ of $X$ in $\mathcal{I}$ is reduced. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U$ be a scheme and let $U \to X$ be a surjective étale morphism. As blowing up commutes with flat base change (Lemma <a href="/tag/085S" data-tag="085S">71.17.3</a>) we can prove each of these statements after base change to $U$. This reduces us to the case of schemes. In this case the result is Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0808" data-tag="0808">31.33.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>